Z||000004||StuGood||02-15-2001||10:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loren:<BR><B>...there is a nipple on the back end where a medium sized vaccum line could be attached.(mine does not have one)...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agree that it sounds like EGR solenoid.<P>I believe the port on the "back" end (towards front of car) ordinarily connects to a steel line on the forward firewall (via a flexible hose), and ultimately goes to the "clean" side of the air cleaner.  I'm pretty certain it's a vent line.<P>On the junkyard EGR solenoid you dissected, perhaps, they put a little foam filter on that port, instead of routing to air cleaner.  That's my guess, anyway.   <P>  ||||reg||14
